#other("Guest", ("I do have one question and it's in regard to –well, I have a lot of questions– But the حِجاب (Hijab: Islamic Veiling) –if I pronounce that correctly– So obviously when one hears the word Hijab, they're thinking of the scarf that women wear on them. Is that what it actually is though? Because from what I've heard, it's sort of a metaphorical thing, That, for women, it means a certain thing. And for men, it means something else?",), cut: true)
