#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Okay. So, I I have a long video that I really recommend people sitting here, especially parents to to watch on my channel. It's about raising your kids, raising your children the right way, the behavior, the attitude. Recommend everybody sitting here to watch that video. Of course, I'm I don't want to give you 1 hour lecture now. I'm going to give you a brief answer, but watch that video. You get a very detailed answer of what I'm about to say. So, the title, I don't remember the title. It has something to do with raising your kids.", "So, uh let me find the exact title right right now. It's a very recent video and it should be very easy to find inshallah. One second. Let me see. Okay. Okay. So, uh yeah, it's if you're doing this, there's a chance your kid leaves Islam. That's the title. Yeah. So, if you're doing what this video says, there's a chance your kid leaves Islam. I'd recommend you watch that. Okay? Because it it highlights the issues that we have, especially in a community like this, which is a western community. There's a lot of problems that parents are doing.", "Now you say how do you get your kid your kids to Yes. The question is how do you get your kids or your children to act upon their knowledge of Islam. The first and most important thing is to be their example. You are a mother. If you don't wear a hijab and you want to say to your daughter, wear it a hijab. She's not going to listen to you. You put makeup on. You spend the entire day watching TV and movies and Korean pop stars and whatever girls are doing these days. And then you're like your to your daughter.", "Oh, read the Quran. Read the Quran. Now, watch the scholar. She's going to look at you. What are you doing? You're not reading the Quran. Last time I've I've seen you holding the Quran for 10 minutes was last Ramadan. Why you telling me read the Quran, read the Quran. You don't do it yourself. It hurts to hear this, but that's the reality. If you are not an