#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("You have to teach your kids their foundations. And learn like, you know, we have so many examples in the Quran and the Sunnah and the Hadith. Like the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam. There's this famous narration from Abdullah ibn Abbas where he said one day he was riding behind the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam. And look how the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam is teaching him and he was a ghulam, he was a young boy. But look how the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam is talking to him. This is how you You need to address your kids. I know I I still remember till this day when my mother, may Allah be pleased with her and preserve her.", "She told me something I still remember in this day when I was a kid. She was telling me about how to to groom and take care of my body and how to trim your hair and stuff. She was telling me until this day I remember because she stood me up and she said, \"Do you know how to do this?\" I said, \"No.\" She said, \"You need to understand as a Muslim we do this. The Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam said this. You need to do this.\" I And until this day, I was a kid, I don't even remember how I looked, but I remember when she told me to do that.", "The Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam told him, \"Oh young boy.\" So look, the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam is addressing him. And then he's saying, \"I'm going to teach you a few words.\" We don't even sometimes talk to each other that way. The Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam is talking as adults. The Prophet is talking to a young boy in this way. He says to him, \"Be watchful of Allah. He will preserve you. If you're watchful of Allah and you obey his command, Allah will protect you. He will safeguard you. Safeguard his rights. He will be always with you.", "If you beg, beg only from Allah.\" Oh look, your your kids now they go, they beg everybody. They would go and beg a random stranger for a piece of candy because you don't teach them. And if you seek assistance, supplicate to Allah alone. Look, these values if you instill in your child when he is in time of difficulty, he's going to remember Allah, he's going to make dua, he's going to call upon Allah. And remember that if all the people gather to benefit you, they will not be able to benefit you except what Allah wants for you.", "Look, look, when the kid understands that. Look, if everybody comes and everybody wants to give me money, everyone wants to help me. If Allah if Allah is not happy with me, if Allah is not pleased with me, if Allah is not willing this, I'm not going to get it. And if everybody comes against me and they try to harm me, if everybody's my enemy, I shouldn't be scared because none of them can do anything to me except for Allah. We have these narrations where the prophet is teaching young kids so we can copy and do the same thing and teach our children.", "We don't just read these narrations, this hadith, these verses for the sake of reading them. Allah tells us in the Quran, you know in Surah in Surah Luqman, I'm sure many of you know. Why Allah gives us an example of how Luqman was teaching and advising his son so you can bring your son and do the same thing. Allah says in the Quran, \"When Luqman said to his son advising him, what we're saying, bringing your children, sitting them down to give them advice, to teach them, 'Oh my son, do not commit shirk with Allah. Do not associate with Allah.", "Indeed, shirk is a grave sin. Oh my son, do not associate with Allah. Worship Allah alone.'\" His young son, he's teaching him, he's giving him these words so he can understand. So he can learn in the future that you instill within your child tawhid. You instill within your child monotheism, not associating with God, not being a polytheist from a very young age. Then he says to him, \"My dear son, were to weigh a mustard seed and it is hidden inside a rock or in all of the heavens or all of the earth, Allah is able to bring it.", "Surely, Allah is the most subtle, the all-aware.\" The kid then internalizes, understands that Allah has the ability, the power over all this universe that he's created. He's able to control everything. So you do not despair when you are in a bad situation. You understand that Allah is the creator, that has the power over everything. Then he talks to him about the deeds, \"Yeah, my son, establish Enjoy my my son, establish the prayer. Enjoy in the good and forbid the evil. And be patient upon that which happens to you. Surely, this is a resolve to aspire to.\"", "And then he says to him, \"And do not turn your nose up to the people. Do not work pridefully on the earth. Allah does not like those who are boastful and arrogant.\" You teach your kid not to be like that from a young age, so he can grow up on these characteristics. Be moderate in your pace. Lower your voice. For indeed, the ugliest of voices is the braying of a donkey. So, when you say these things, when you teach your kid from a very very young age, this is the characteristics. This is the behavior that you take.", "This is the foundations that you believe in. We are Muslims because of the following. Islam is the truth. Prophet Muhammad was a messenger from God. He was sent to mankind. Allah chose Prophet Muhammad because of his pure heart. And Allah sent all of these prophets and messengers because Allah loves us, wants to take us out from misguidance into guidance, into light. And he gives us all of these commands cuz these commands are for our benefit. Allah doesn't benefit from it. We are the ones who benefit from it. We do them because they are beneficial for us.", "And then you give them examples of when someone makes something, they tell you how to interact with it because they know what's best for it. They created it. Allah created us. He knows what's best for us. Then you teach your kid why you're Muslims, why we believe what we believe. And you make a connection between them and their creator. You have to regularly sit down your sit your kids down and teach them this. You teach them this belief that to rely on Allah alone. And to teach them, of course, the basics of of their practices.", "That you need to know yourself how to pray, when is your breaking, when is not your you do is not breaking, what is the ark end of the prayer. You need to teach your kids these things. You need to grow up with the correct foundation because once they're sponge is filled, then you don't worry about other influences influencing them because they know. They grew up knowing that Allah is the only true God. They understand that there is no other gods out there. They understand why they're believers. They understand why they pray to Allah. They understand why Islam is the truth.", "Then you give them role models. When you give your kid the phone, his role model becomes this random YouTuber. You have to give him a role model. How do you give him a role model? Of course, first, you have to be a good example in their life. But teach your kid the stories of the Sahaba. Teach your kid the stories of the prophets. Teach your kid the stories of the companions. And when you teach them, you teach them a value in the story. You teach them the the courageous nature of Ali ibn Abi Talib in his battles.", "You teach them the wisdom of the Sahaba, Abu Bakr as-Siddiq. You teach them the strength of Umar ibn al-Khattab. And you bring them a story. There is many examples that we we have. And this has to be regular. At the very least minimum, once a week. Then a kid starts to look up to someone. And then when you teach them the value, when that same situation happens to them, they remember. I have to be honorable because Ali ibn Abi Talib was honorable. Because Uthman ibn Affan was honorable. I should be honorable in this situation. This Sahabi forgave the other Sahabi when he did this to him.", "I should forgive my friend when my friend does that does something bad to me or curses me or insults me. These values are only going to come from these stories and these role models that you build in your child's life. Once your child has a role model they look up to, they will want to imitate. They will want to do the same thing they did. They will want to learn more about them. That is not going to come on its own. You have to do that. You have to put that effort as a parent. Have to put the effort.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"If You're Doing This, There's A Chance Your Kid Leaves Islam! Muhammed Ali\"")

