#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("And I'm telling you, I'm telling you these things to do before it is too late. You will be responsible on the day of judgment for what your kids do if you don't teach them. If you don't take your responsibility and put the effort in and do everything in your power, Allah will hold you accountable for how they ended up. So, I'm telling you this before it's too late. Before you become that person that, \"Oh, let me book a call. Let me get a private session because my son left Islam or my daughter become like this or my son has become like that.", "Well, they will become like this if you don't teach them the foundations. So, before it is too late, you got to wake up. You got to understand it is time now for us to put some effort as parents to sit down seriously. Look, session I I I was having not too long ago. The parents were crying. They were sitting down like, \"We're realizing.\" But, realizing when? When it's too late? Oh, we should have been doing this. We realized that we were wrong. You cannot go back in time. So, do not be the parent who leaves his kids without guidance, without role models, without teachers, and not instilling the right values in them from a a young age.", "Teach your kid the right beliefs, the right creed that we have as Muslims, the right behaviors, and have role models for them. And make sure these phones, these devices are not given. These devices should only be given for call. You know, give them a a Nokia phone or something like that. When they're elder, once they have the correct foundations, the correct beliefs, you're you're sure that they're understanding, they're good, then maybe you can introduce these devices into the life. Never ever introduce these devices for young kids. Never ever introduce these social media devices and phones and tablets for your kid when he's 7, 8, 9, 10, or 11 years old.", "Never. Wait until your kid has already been established in the right beliefs, in the right foundation, in the right understanding. He's smarter. He understands the right from wrong. Then perhaps you can gradually start to introduce these devices. And if you've already done this, then you have to slowly and slowly apply what we said you need to do, and slowly restrict that usage in their life. It'll be very difficult because now you've made their life on their phone because you were doing bad parenting. But, if you want your kids to be good in the future, do not go in the complete path of destruction, then start applying the right teachings.", "It will make an influence even if your kids grew up with these things slowly by slowly. Make a few restrictions on the usages, introduce the beliefs, them understanding what they believe. Even if they go astray a little bit, there's always a foundation to they can come back to. May Allah Azza Wajjal guide us all and guide our kids, and guide our families to the best of mannerisms and best of deeds and that which pleases him. May Allah Azza Wajjal give you all baraka and your families and Inshallah you listen to this and you will start applying it in your life Inshallah. Assalamualaikum Warahmatullahi",))
