#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("So we have a serious crisis in the Muslim community today and this crisis is not being talked about enough and that is the marriage crisis. There's general overall marriage crisis in the world today but especially within the Muslim community. And I get a lot of messages from brothers and sisters alike that they're doing many things wrong or they have done many things wrong and they're struggling to get married. Now some of them haven't done anything wrong but they're also struggling to get married. So everyone is struggling to get married. It's very important that we highlight these issues that we have as a community so we can attempt to fix it.", "So we can attempt to stop contributing towards this crisis that is causing a lot of damage and harm in our community. And the people who are causing this crisis are the parents, the women that are trying to get married and the men that are trying to get married. So I'm going to highlight the things that each of them is doing wrong. The prophet wasallam there's a hadith where he says if someone comes to you and you accept his religion, he has a good religion, he has good manners, then get him married. If you do not do this, then there will be great corruption in the land.", "Now there are some scholars that weaken this narration and there is a debate over the authenticity of it. However, its meaning is for sure correct. If marriage stops becoming about someone has good religion and good characteristics and worthy of marriage and starts becoming about other worldly matters and worldly things then great corruption will spread because if people do not get married then they are going to resort to haram. So what are the issues? What are we doing to contribute towards this crisis that we have? So the first thing I'm going to start with is I'm going to start talking about the parents.", "Why am I going to start talking about the parents? Because the parents are the core. If the parents are doing things correctly, then that will influence their children and by extension that will solve majority of the issues that we're having today. However, a lot of these issues are related to the parents. So, I'm going to start with the parents, then I'm going to talk about the women, and then I'm going to talk about the men. So, the first thing I'm going to talk about is the idea of raising your kids. The parents are not raising their kids, teaching them the importance of marriage and family.", "They're not teaching them the necessary skills and the necessary things that they would need so they can be a desirable spouse, man or woman. The parents are not teaching the men to be responsible, to be strong, to be intelligent, to be able to protect and provide, to have the correct attributes of men, which is to keep your word, not to be a liar, to be courageous. We're not teaching our kids that. And we're not teaching them the importance of marriage as an idea is like how important is it in Islam or in religion or in your life to have one of your priorities to get married as soon as you can so you can protect yourself from the fa.", "The parents are not doing this. They're not doing this job of teaching the importance and the necessary skills. A lot of the sisters today and a lot of the brothers today do not have the skills. This is a massive problem that we have. And what are the parents focusing on? They're focusing on what and the west have told them. This piece of paper everything is about education. Why? Because Allahel says on the Quran this life, this is about mutual boosting. My son is an engineer. My daughter is a doctor. My son is this. My daughter is that.", "Parents care about boosting themselves to other parents rather than caring about what is the benefit and what is important for the future of the children. And this applies both to men and women. However, it's more important in the case of the girls and I'm going to talk about that later towards the end of the video. However, it applies to both. This idea of making it important in the mind of your child the idea of marriage and that this is a very core fundamental thing in their life that they should seek they should have the necessary skills for and that you give them the requirement and teach them what is necessary and needed for them to have these skills so they can get married.", "Now another very important thing that the parents are doing which is horrendous which is the idea of stopping their kids from getting married when they're young. I get many messages from sisters and brothers alike. They want to get married. They're young. They can be in their mid to late teens or they can be in early 20s. Whatever their age is, they want to get married. They have a desire. They want to get married. And the parents are just like, \"You're too young. You're young. You're young. You're too young.\" And it's good sisters and good brothers and they seem to be willing to get married.", "They're mature enough to get married from how they speak. However, the parents are like, \"Oh, no, no, you're young.\" Some parents are like, I they just want to keep their kids with them for longer. Some parents are like this. Some of the parents are just careless. I don't want to deal with all of these issues. I'm just going to say you're young. Come back later. And the prophetat wasam he said, \"Oh young people, whoever of you is able to get married, let him get married.\" Why did they say, \"Oh young people specifically.\" And then the prophetam he said who cannot let him fast because it's going to be protecting him from what?", "From the desire. The prophet wasallam is giving this advice to the young men and women because the prophet wasallam knows that the desire is there in this specific age. the desire is more amplified than anything else. So when you go tell your kid, \"Oh, you're too young. Just go.\" You're leading your child to go do and later you come and say, \"Why is my daughter with this random boyfriend or my son is dating this girl?\" Why? Why? Because the kid wants to get married. You have not talked seriously with your kid. You have not put the effort to get them married when they're young.", "All what you're thinking about is like, \"I don't want to deal with this right now. Couldn't care less. focus on your own self as if your children are not important. So you are contributing towards this crisis that we have because you are preventing a lot of these men and women from getting married in a age when they are desiring the marriage and then they end up getting attached in haram relationships and years and years go by and then they don't get married and they start having trauma and we have a million issue in the community just because you are preventing your own kids from getting married.", "Then we have the idea of asking ridiculous amounts of money right when the man is coming for your daughter or like okay go bring me 100 200k bring me a car complicating everything in the marriage I want this wedding to be like this and that and all of it is coming from what what we said about boosting this mutual boosting oh your cousin she had the biggest wedding in the entire city so you need to have a similar wedding or you shouldn't get married for them they don't care like the husband could later on do something do all types of things that are wrong to the girl.", "But as long as he does the stupid wedding and they can boost to their other stupid people in the community, then they're like happy. Of course, I'm not going to address every issue out there. I'm going to just address what I think are the most important serious ones. However, this is one of the most serious issues which prevents people from getting married. I know many men and and I'm talking about now I'm talking about my experience with a lot of men and women that are struggling to get married and what they say is the issues that they're facing because they go a man was trying to get married he's not poor and he's not rich he's okay however like you got in some communities in that committee with gold and silver and like they're asking him for this asking and the brother is like struggling to get married he can't get", "married he can take care of the family he can look after his kids however he cannot fulfill these ridiculous less requirements to do with weddings and to do with money and to do with all of these things that this person did and you're not doing. So these parents need to wake up. You want to sell your daughter as a piece of clothing. You want someone that destroys the the life of your daughter later on just because you are able to boost for another parent. So you got to wake up as parents. You got to put the priority, the mannerisms, the dean of the individual that is coming to marry your daughter before everything else.", "That is the first thing that you need to put. Now parents as well, both father and the mother are not putting effort as well to find spouses for their kids. They're not putting any effort trying to see in the community seek if there is people that they know in in the similar age and they probably know many families that have people in similar ages. However, they're not putting effort. And I'm going to this is general, but it's specifically about the fathers as well because it's the father's job to put effort to find someone for his daughter.", "And then the sisters, they come later and they speak to me and they're like in their 30s or whatever going to get married and say, \"Does your father put any effort?\" No, he didn't really. He wasn't concerned. I wasn't concerned. So, he wasn't concerned. So, the fathers are not even putting any effort. They're expecting their daughter to go and like find some random man in the street and come like, \"Okay, here I want to marry this person.\" What are we are we going to pretend that we're kufu? We're going to deal like them or what?", "It is your responsibility as a father to put effort. Of course, it is permissible for a Muslim woman if she finds the right person that somehow she reaches out in an indirect way and tries to get him to speak to her father. I'm not saying this is haram so long as it's within Islamic bounds and is done correctly. However, that is not what majority of sisters are going to do. number one and number two that is not their responsibility in the first place but it is mainly the responsibility of the father to put that effort and try and find for his daughters we know in the Quran Mus Alisam when he was presented he told him I will give you one of my two daughters in marriage why is he presenting his daughters he sees a man who's worthy Mus Alam's a prophet of god he's worthy and he has right character right religion so", "he is presenting his daughters because that is his responsibility as a father. The daughters didn't come and say, \"Oh, we want to marry you.\" They came, they said, \"Our father, he wants something from you. He wants to have a word with you.\" That's it. They connected him with Daharam and then he spoke to them. So that is your responsibility as a father. Don't just sit down and wait like this and then tomorrow you're going to come and cry when your daughter is going with this guy, with Max, with Jonathan, with whatever behind the bush. It's your fault.", "You're not putting any effort. The desire is there at the kids and you're not doing any work as parents to get your children married in the right age when they have that desire when they are looking for marriage. Now also you have the idea of putting the culture the parents and many communities putting the culture over the religion. Oh, we're only going to marry from our cousin's family or this family or this ethnicity. They would reject people. Oh, this person is a revert. I'm going to reject him. Oh, this man is from Somalia or Athubia or whatever.", "I'm going to reject him. Doesn't matter if he has the right religion, the right character, whatever. No, it's about a lot of racism and a lot of cultural ignorance that are being applied and it is preventing a lot of good marriages even though the sisters agree and the brothers agreeing but the parents are the ones who are coming and preventing that marriage for all of these cultural reason. Many of the scholars have advised against close very close marriage which you have in many communities rather than branching out and looking for who is the most suitable.", "They just want to own. It has to be from our tribe. No. Allah says he made us into different nations and tribes so we can get to know each other. Prophetam he said there's no superiority of a white over a black or a black over white. It's it's about your piety. This is what you need to look for. Also that parents putting their ego over the benefits of the kids. Sometimes there's a good man and a good woman. They want to get married and they're both agreeing. and they're both okay, everything is good, but this parent has an issue with the parent of the boy or this mother has an issue with the other mother.", "The marriage is not about you, it's about them. If they're agreeing with each other, they both have good character and religion. Fix your issues. Put your step on your ego and put the benefit of your children first. So these are I would say the main issues that I'm seeing. There's of course other issues, but these are some of the main issues that are to do with the parents specifically. what we are doing as parents to contribute more and more towards this crisis. I want you to understand this crisis, it destroys communities. Because when we don't have families, which is the foundation of the community, the foundation of everything, then you don't have the kids being raised correctly.", "You have everybody doing haram. You have children born out of wedlock. You have people caring about the duny. We have nothing. We have no community. If we don't have a family, we don't have a community. So, we're talking about something serious that we are contributing and every day we're leading into more and more problems in our community. We need to fix this. We need to work on this.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"The Muslim Marriage Crisis: Causes, Effects & Solutions | Muhammed Ali\"")

=== 58.6 The marriage crisis: delayed marriage and expectations
// NODE P13.C04.S06
// EXCERPT ML009 199-253
// T ML009 199,200,201,202,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223,224,225,226,227,228,229,230,231,232,233,234,235,236,237,238,239,240,241,242,243,244,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,252,253 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now I'm going to move on to the women in the community. So what are the main issues that we see with the sisters in the community that are also contributing to this marriage crisis that we're dealing with? The first thing I'm going to highlight is the idea of unrealistic expectations. And this comes a lot of it is influenced by social media. A lot of sisters are on social media. They watch a lot of nonsense. They watch a lot of seriouses, dramas, this that follow this actress, this person, that person. And their expectation is like, \"Oh, I want to go to the Hawaii.", "I want a guy that looks like Brad Pit. I want him to be like this. I want him to be like that.\" All of these nonsensical, unrealistic expectations. And they don't look at someone in their level. They don't look at someone who's mukaf, who's in the same level as themselves. No, they're just like they think they can get something that doesn't exist, only exists in movies. A lot of sisters have this issue and it's influenced by social media, like I said, because of what they see. But not only that, it's also because we get a lot of women on social media and you get men, a lot of like stupid men messaging them and oh, you know, showing desire in them and whatever.", "So they think that like, you know what, there's a millions of options out there. And majority of these friends are a bunch of losers, of course, because that's what they're doing. They wouldn't be doing this if unless they're a bunch of losers. And also, they're not interested in marrying you and taking care of you. None of that. They just want to do a specific thing. That's all what they want. But it gives this wrong perception in the mind of women that look, oh, there's a million men I can choose from. And they don't these are all men they wouldn't want to marry anyways.", "But it gives them this issue which leads their ego and gives them this unrealistic expectations where they think they can marry like no the president of the country. No, we got to look for what is suitable for us and our priority should be the dean, should be the religion, should be the mannerisms, should be the person that fears Allah because if he fears Allah, he will fear Allah in dealing with you. He will look after you, he'll take care of you. He wouldn't do something bad to you because he fears Allah and he cares about his religion and he has morals that should be your priority.", "Not the other unrealistic expectations that you are influenced by watching social media. Now also the idea which upsets many people but the idea of you have the women putting their career or education as a priority over marriage. Nobody's telling you don't get educated ever this piece of paper is not the foundation of your life. This kafir that made you think that this piece of paper is the end all be all. It is not wall it is not. We talk to the sisters and lot of sisters don't understand. I get many messages from sisters that are 34, 35 and they all talk about how much they regret that they haven't started seeking marriage earlier and they left everything just focusing on career, focusing on this, focusing on that and now they cannot find a spouse now they cannot get married because they didn't put it as a priority.", "They didn't care. They're like, I'm going to just focus on this and I'm not going to focus on that. If all your energy is being put towards career and education and you don't have marriage at all in your mind, you will end up wasting and wasting years of your life and in the end it is going to be very difficult for you to get married. So this idea of putting the career first, we're not telling you like I said do not get educated, do not work in a halal way with the Islamic requirement. Nobody's saying this.", "However, we're talking about priorities. They don't have to be against each other. But you a priority should be marriage over education. A priority should be marriage over a career. That should be something as a priority for you because you will want it sooner or later. However, it will not be easier for you to do later on.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"The Muslim Marriage Crisis: Causes, Effects & Solutions | Muhammed Ali\"")
#sep()
// EXCERPT ML196 149-221
// T ML196 149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Her priority shouldn't be the priority of a lot of women in the West: The feministic priority of my career, right! And then they say, for instance, I'm going to get married in my 30s I'm going to start thinking about marriage when I'm 35 And in reality, OK, you're going to start thinking about marriage when you're 35 but you're not going to be desired by the opposite gender when you're 35 And they don't realise that, they don't understand that because they think men and women are the same thing in their mind, OK? \"Oh, yeah, I like men that are older than me\", therefore, men will like women that are older than them!", "No, it doesn't work like that. Because we're opposite genders,we have different attractions Like the men would always be attracted to lower girls that are younger –we're speaking in general, of course– and women will be attracted to older And that is where the harmony comes in If both of them are attracted to older, the society will not even function! And as I said, when it comes to fertility and these things, these are biological things, A woman hits the age of 30, 80% of her eggs are gone when she's 35, 90%. And then you start going into high-risk pregnancy in which there is damage, It can be on the child or the mother's health.", "These are biological realities now. Someone might be \"oh, I don't like this\", But I'm sorry, this is the truth. This is the reality, I cannot change human biology reality for you So they can put their career first. And what ends up doing is they spend their life doing that thing, working, stressing, completely miserable! And they reach an age, sadly, they reach an age in which they realise that's too late When it's time to realise that, maybe in the end of the 20s, beginning of 30s And I cannot tell you how many people I've seen And I've seen a lot of applications for people who try to get married and stuff like that.", "And I've seen always a common theme. The overwhelming majority of the women that are not married, are trying to get married, Are at the end of their 20s, beginning of their 30s plus,",))
// T ML196 182 | Alejandro | dash:182 | cut:0
#other("Alejandro", ("And these applications are like what context?",))
// T ML196 183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215 | The Muslim Lantern | dash:183 | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("so you have something..Yeah, and in different contexts, let's just say.. I don't want to get into too many details, but let's just say there are websites, for example, there are Apps, And I try to look at and collect data. There are websites, there are apps, there are mosques, where people sometimes put resumes, they're trying to get married So they try to connect people with each other, right! So I'm talking about looking at this data, looking at this information, look at the people that I interact with generally, this has always been the case And these women will have degrees actually, a lot of them will have degrees, but sometimes the degree can actually be an obstacle Because when a woman reaches a certain level of education and intelligence, Also the type of partner that she looks for; changes.", "She wants someone who's more intelligent than herself Someone who can actually engage in a conversation, tell her information she doesn't know, Has more experience than herself, all of this stuff. And if this is the case, then doors start closing for her For the other types of people that have not had this level of education, do not have a master's degree, do not have a PhD, whatever she did in her higher education that she was seeking. So all of these things are just facts and realities. we're not telling anyone what to do. People will do and make their own decisions in life And in the end, we're just telling them things from experience.", "We're telling them what we see, how the reality actually works. Now someone can take that advice. Someone can say \"oh, no, I don't care, I want to seek\" Go ahead, seek all the higher education you want to seek. Become the most knowledgeable, intelligent person and put your career as a priority That's up to you. You can do that. No one is going to stop you or tell you not to do it In the end, we're giving advice for people who are looking for advice For people who are looking for information and advice that would benefit them Someone who is not, that's up to them",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"Agnostic Questions Muslim On The Education Of Women In Islam! Muhammed Ali\"")
#sep()
