// T ML009 254,255,256,257,258,259,260,261,262,263,264,265,266,267,268,269,270,271,272,273,274,275,276,277,278,279,280,281,282,283,284,285,286,287,288,289,290,291,292,293,294,295,296,297,298,299,300,301,302,303,304,305,306,307,308,309,310,311,312,313,314,315,316,317,318,319,320,321,322,323,324,325,326,327,328,329,330,331,332,333,334,335,336,337,338,339,340,341,342,343,344,345,346,347,348,349,350,351,352,353,354,355,356,357,358,359,360,361,362,363,364,365,366,367,368,369,370,371,372,373,374,375,376,377,378,379,380,381,382,383,384,385 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Now, of course, a lot of what sisters are being told is like, \"Oh, I'm just going to care about marriage and I'm not going to work and I'm not going to get money. What if I get divorced? What's going to happen to me?\" This is kind of the most popular idea that is being pushed in the minds of our sisters that is preventing a lot of them from focusing on marriage another focusing on their career education whatever because of this idea. Now nobody enters something with the intention of failing in it. We don't get in the car say what if I get in an accident so I'm I'm not going to get in a car because I could get in an accident.", "I'm not going to get in a plane because I could get in an accident. I'm not going to study and go into the exam because I could fail. There is risk in everything in life. There is risk in everything you do. However, if you take the right precautions and find the right spouse and do whatever is in your capacity and be a righteous wife and rely on Allah, where is Allah in the picture? Where is the reliance on Allah? Isn't Allahel there to protect you? Also, what is this idea as if we don't have families?", "As if you don't have a brother, as if you don't have a father who can look after you as well. If you got divorced, as if like if you got divorced, everyone else disappears. No, people don't disappear. You have a family that can look after you. But most important thing, you have allahel. And like I said, nobody is telling you don't get educated. Nobody is telling you you don't work. You can get educated then get married. You can be married and work in halal and save money. So nobody is telling you don't do that. You could work for your husband.", "You could work with your husband and make money and if something happens, you have your money. It's not for him to take. However, that shouldn't be the reason we say I'm not going to get married because what if I get divorced? This what if opens the door of the shaitan as the prophetam said it's just a trick of the shaitan that is being played now and a lot of the women in our community are falling for so we need to start waking up and understanding that marriage should be put as a priority it is something that allahel says in the Quran he's the one who created for you from yourself spouses so you can have this peace and tranquility and he made between you mercy and love this is our nature both as men and women we can all both pretend oh I don't want to get married that's a", "bunch of we're just tricking yourself that they will come and you will come and say when it is too late I want to get married I feel alone but you need to start doing this earlier now a lot of these sisters will have better sisters around them wrong friend group better why are they better because many of these women have done many haram things and had many bad experiences with men of them are older they're unable to get married and they say misery loves company so they do two things first they want to keep you from getting married because then they feel like you know what it's not only me I'm not getting married, you're also not getting married.", "And a lot of women are envious like that. They don't want you to get married so they can feel better about themselves that look, it's not just me, I'm not get married, but you're also not married. So that's one thing that they're doing. This idea of trying to make more people like themselves. The second thing that they're doing is giving you all of these stories. Oh, look, I got married and this happened and this woman got married and this happened to her. So don't get married because this may happen to you as well. So they start making them hate marriage.", "And a lot of sisters what they do is they generalize ideas the personal experiences they start generalizing. If this happened to someone then it will happen to me as well. No there is bad experiences in everything in life. If we start applying just because a person had bad experience in something they were not going to do it nobody's going to do anything. So it's very important that you look at are the friends in your group. Are they encouraging you to get married to find happiness or are they envious of you and they're trying to put you down and bring you to the same company that they have.", "And then you have this idea of like I want to find myself phase, you know, it's like I'm lost in the kitchen and I'm gonna go find myself like I'm not here. I'm gonna go find myself. This like I need to find the stage of finding myself. She's like the most like craziest things I've heard, but it is widespread. I have issues I need to work on. I'm not going to get married until I fix myself. Nobody is perfect. Nobody gets married and they have like the perfect personality or everything goes well. Nobody. Everyone when they get married, you will have something that you don't like in your spouse.", "Every spouse will have issues. And that is the reality of life. You're not going to find yourself because you are yourself. So there is nothing to find. There's no idea of finding yourself. If by finding yourself you mean that you're going to fix every issue that you have, it will never happen. Everybody has issues. So, it's about being cautious of the issues that you have, working on yourself, which everybody does, and being honest with whoever the partner is that you're going to marry of the issues that you have. So, they can be upfront as well with you and both of you can be on the same page and then that doesn't lead to other issues, future issues in the future.", "So, this is what you need to understand. Now, a lot of women as well are being sold this idea, oh, you're too young to get married. Like I said, they're told by many other women that are better or they're told by friends or whatever. Oh, you're too young to get married. Like I said prophetam he said oh young people whoever of you is able to get married let him get married and a lot of sisters don't like hearing this but we say to them that when men look to get married if you want the best chance to get the best spouse to get the most amount of people that you can get married to so you can get the best spouse you can be happier in your life then you need to look earlier because it takes time to find people especially in this day and age and because when men look for women, they look for women that are in a childbearing age.", "When men come and I ask, \"What are you looking for?\" They say, \"Childbearing age.\" Right? In other words, a sister that is younger in her age. A lot of sisters, okay, you might not like this. A lot of sisters may be listening and they're like older in age and they're not happy listening to this, so they're going to put a comment. Oh, how could you say this? It's the reality. Nobody can change the reality. Whether we like the reality or we don't like the reality, that is the reality. A man wants to get married. He wants to have kids, wants to have healthy kids.", "He wants his wife to have an easier pregnancy. It's natural. He want his wife to be younger so she can look after the kids and have more energy around the kids. So the men are looking for that. Now if you as a sister did not get married and you're older, nobody is saying that you're not going to get married. You will find someone inshallah. However, I'm talking about how likely you are and how easier it is and why you need to look when you're younger and leave this idea of like, oh, I'm too young to get married.", "No, you're not too young. As long as you are in an age where you have desires, there is a fitna. If you're not getting married, you will get all sorts of wolves around you trying to get to know you and one day you will fall for the trick. You didn't get married, you'll end up doing something else, something haram, because everybody has desires, men and women. Then you have the opposite of that, which you have some women telling girls, oh, you got to start dating and freeing so you can find the husband. You know, you're wearing a hijab, take it back a little bit.", "Show some of your hair so then you can find the husband. Take your hijab completely off so you can start attracting the opposite gender. Start going to here to the club and the bar and this person and this place and that place so you can find the husband. You're not going to find the husband by being a righteous sister who goes to the mall and dresses. This is being widespread. That's the the other extreme that we see in the community. And yeah, you will attract a lot more men like this, but you're going to attract the men that don't want to marry you.", "You're going to attract the men that you don't want to marry. You're going to attract the men that want to use you and move on to the next one. You're going to attract trauma. You're going to attract baggage. You're going to attract everything evil because you try to seek something that Allah is not pleased with because you use something that Allah is not pleased with to seek marriage and you will end up regretting everything you do. And like I there's so many experiences I can talk about sisters coming. Remember the sister that came she's a rever she brought a person with her.", "They they were dating before marriage and she became pregnant and that's why now they want to get married and I said to her not to marry him. I told her you regret this. She came two years later and they divorced and now she has a kid and that's it. She has a kid and she got married while she had a chance not to get married but now she got married and wasted years from her life. Now she has the kid and she's divorced. Because you start with something haram, you build a relationship with someone in a haram way, they're not going to fear Allah with you because you started with them in the wrong way.",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"The Muslim Marriage Crisis: Causes, Effects & Solutions | Muhammed Ali\"")

